  data:  # 60c0
    kind: work_item  # 60c0
    title: "ruby: a namespaced external constant whose last segment names a project class (Prometheus::Client) is treated as that class"  # 60c0
    status: todo_hard  # 60c0
    priority: 3  # 60c0
    parent:  # 60c0
    tags:  # 60c0
    - ruby  # 60c0
    - call_graph  # 60c0
    - analysis_quality  # 60c0
    isbefore: []  # 60c0
    duplicate_of: []  # 60c0
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 60c0
    pr_ref:  # 60c0
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 closing WI-johib (PR #1279). ruby's _try_receiver_call tries a scope_resolution receiver's SHORT NAME as a candidate (Prometheus::Client -> 'Client'), and ruby symbol names carry no namespace (a class Client in any module is named 'Client'). So an EXTERNAL namespaced constant whose last segment matches a project class is treated as that class. Measured on postal after #1279: Prometheus::Client.registry -> project Client -> the inherited-calls linker -> HasPrometheusMetrics.registry, a wrong binding (1 site on postal; 0 on chatwoot).\n\nFIX SHAPE (not built): take the short-name candidate only when the full name cannot be external. For example, require that the leading namespace segment ('Prometheus') is itself a project module, or record the namespace on class symbols (meta) and compare it. Measure on postal and chatwoot. WI-surar (the lowercased module slot) is adjacent: it is about the external spelling, not the binding."  # 60c0
    fields: {}  # 60c0
- op: discuss  # 016a
  at: '2026-10-01T12:22:26Z'  # 016a
  by: agent  # 016a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 016a
  clock: 2  # 016a
  nonce: 016a  # 016a
  message: "BEARING from WI-surar (branch jgstern-agent/fix/surar, local commit d5e987abce, not merged): the ruby constant-external fallback now spells the module slot as the receiver constant AS WRITTEN (Prometheus::Client::Counter, not counter). So once this item routes a namespaced external constant whose last segment names a project class away from the project-owner path, the fallback will carry the full Prometheus::Client... owner path with no further change. Measured on postal with the branch: Prometheus::Client::Counter.new -> slot Prometheus::Client::Counter. This item's own defect (short-name capture by a project class) is NOT changed by WI-surar: the project_owners check in _try_receiver_call still includes the short name for a scope_resolution receiver."  # 016a
- op: discuss  # 3d33
  at: '2026-10-03T17:07:51Z'  # 3d33
  by: agent  # 3d33
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3d33
  clock: 3  # 3d33
  nonce: 3d33  # 3d33
  message: "PYTHON SIBLING FILED as WI-ratid-mokat-fifon-hiros-nazun-bozim-mojak-jasin: the core inheritance linker binds Python's dotted external base unittest.TestCase by its last segment to Django's in-tree TestCase, closing an inheritance cycle (TestCase -> TransactionTestCase -> SimpleTestCase -> TestCase) that makes the C3 walker refuse every class under Django's test hierarchy (2098 same-file inherited call sites measured on the django corpus repo). Same mechanism as this item (last segment of a namespaced external name taken as a project class, no import context in the linker); a shared fix in inheritance.py's lookup_names fallback may cover both."  # 3d33
